title: '[pallet-revive] Charge the EIP-2565 modexp cost when the modulus length is zero'
doc:
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    The modexp precompile returned an empty output for a zero-length modulus without charging
    its own EIP-2565 cost. The caller still paid the precompile call base cost and the input
    decode. Calls with a zero-length modulus are now charged the EIP-2565 cost like every other
    input, which matches geth and revm. Contracts calling modexp with a zero-length modulus see
    higher gas usage, and such calls can now run out of gas. An exponent longer than 32 bytes
    whose first 32 bytes are zero was also undercharged by one iteration. It now counts
    `8 * (exp_len - 32)` iterations as EIP-198 specifies, so these calls cost more for any modulus
    length. No migration is needed.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
